// Dead-code elimination: emit only what the program can reach.
//
// This is not an optimisation, it is what makes a standard library affordable.
// idstd is merged into EVERY program, so without this a hello-world pays for
// all of it. Measured on a synthetic library of trivial functions, before this
// existed: 243 functions cost 0.36 s and a 33 KB binary against 0.18 s and
// 16 KB with none, and 729 cost 0.75 s and 75 KB. A real standard library is
// several hundred functions with real bodies.
//
// Two rules, both shared with idc.py's prune_unreachable, and the C the two
// emit has to stay byte-identical:
//
//   * This runs AFTER every check, never before -- see guarded_emit. A dead
//     function still has to obey the action limit, the nesting limit and every
//     type rule. Code that stops being checked because nothing calls it is how
//     a library rots, and it would stop checking a user's own dead code too.
//   * A program with no `main` is a library, compiled to a .o, and every one of
//     its functions is an entry point. Nothing is pruned there -- which is what
//     the `main` test below is for. It cannot be asked of the reachable set
//     instead, because init_reach seeds that with "main" whether or not the
//     program has one.
//
// The reachable set is `rfn`, already computed by chk_dead during checking; is_reach
// reads it. `asm` functions are not in the program list at all and are
// unaffected, which is the conservative answer and the right one.
//
// Exported globals are deliberately NOT pruned. An export declared by a
// function nothing calls costs one never-assigned C global -- nothing can read
// it, because chk_dead has already rejected a reachable read of one.

dce_prune() {
  if(find_str((import fnames), "main") >= 0) {
    dce_pack(0, 0);
  }
} return void;

// Compact the program list over itself, keeping the reachable functions in
// their original order, then drop the tail that is left over. `prog` is an
// exported list, so it is rewritten in place through lset and pop rather
// than rebuilt -- only its declaring function may assign it.
//
// The two loops are one function because a block may hold three actions and
// this holds two: splitting them would cost a function whose only job is to
// call the other.
dce_pack(int i, int n) {
  while(i < len((import prog))) {
    n = dce_keep(i, n);
    i = i + 1;
  }
  while(len((import prog)) > n) {
    pop((import prog));
  }
} return int n;

// Keep slot i by writing it at n, the next free slot. n only advances when
// something was kept, which is what makes this a compaction rather than a copy.
dce_keep(int i, int n) {
  string s1_of_v = s1_of((import prog)[i]);
  if(is_reach(s1_of_v) == 1) {
    lset((import prog), n, (import prog)[i]);
    n = n + 1;
  }
} return int n;
